# Wrong output (PLAN.md): `lo` and `hi`, declared without `%`, are
# parsed as symbols, so `mov.b32 %r2, {lo, hi}` reads no register, %r2
# is taken as the same in every thread, and the store runs on a whole
# warp or none. Only thread 0 runs it: 1 sector.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/bare_registers.ptx | FileCheck "%s"
CHECK: kernel micro_bare_registers
CHECK: st.global.u32  global store 4 B (predicated)  warp: 4–5 sectors (ideal 4)
